	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: The paper developed a self-explaining neural network, the Partial Response Network, and benchmarked it against the previously published deep learning IHTSA model, IMPACT, and EBM. Inputs were tabular recipient and donor variables. The main study design was a temporal derivation/tuning/validation framework: 1997–2013 for training, 2014–2016 for testing/hyperparameter optimization, and 2017–2018 as blinded external validation. Explainability was intrinsic to the PRN design through explicit partial-response functions rather than SHAP/LIME, but it still meets the user’s category of explainability used.  ￼

